+# Keep SMS for pickup reminders
+
+For whoever is asked to switch pickup reminders to email to save the SMS cost. Reminders stay on SMS, because email
+was tried and missed pickups nearly doubled.
+
+## Context
+
+SMS reminders cost about 40 euros a month, and volunteers have proposed switching to email at least three times
+(most recently [issue 52](../../notes/issue-52.md)) since it is free. Larder ran that experiment from April to June
+2025: the provider's report showed 34% of reminder emails were never opened, and missed pickups rose from 6% of
+pantry orders to 13%. Many members share one household phone and do not check email, but see SMS. Every missed
+pickup is a packed bag whose fresh food is thrown out by closing time. Larder switched back to SMS on July 1, 2025,
+and missed pickups were back to 6% by August.
+
+## Options
+
+- **Email**: free; tried April-June 2025 and reverted, because missed pickups rose from 6% to 13%.
+- **SMS**: chosen.
+
+## Decision
+
+Pickup reminders stay on SMS, because the 40-euro monthly cost is less than the fresh food lost to the missed
+pickups email caused.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Larder keeps paying for SMS. Anyone proposing email again should read this ADR first; the missed-pickup data from the
+2025 trial is in [issue 52](../../notes/issue-52.md).
